## TDD Approach Demonstrated

Following strict **RED-GREEN-REFACTOR** cycle:

1. **RED Phase**: Wrote failing tests first
   - Tests for non-existent classes compilation failure
   - Tests expecting validation failures

2. **GREEN Phase**: Implemented minimal code to pass tests
   - [ArbitrageOpportunity](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/domain/ArbitrageOpportunity.java#28-169) with validation logic
   - [ArbitrageRepository](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/ArbitrageRepository.java#18-51) with Spring Data JPA
   - [ArbitrageServiceImpl](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/service/impl/ArbitrageServiceImpl.java#40-132) with BigDecimal calculations

3. **REFACTOR Phase**: Enhanced code quality
   - Added comprehensive javadoc
   - Fixed timestamp precision issue (PostgreSQL microseconds)
   - Removed unused imports

---

## Design Principles Applied

### SOLID
- **Single Responsibility**: Each class has one clear purpose
- **Dependency Inversion**: Service depends on abstractions ([PriceService](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/service/PriceService.java#10-29), [ArbitrageRepository](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/repository/ArbitrageRepository.java#18-51))
- **Interface Segregation**: [ArbitrageService](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/service/ArbitrageService.java#19-48) interface with focused methods

### DRY
- Reused existing patterns from [PriceTick](file:///home/pranay/anotherDrive/javaCodes/crypto-price-aggregator/src/main/java/com/cryptoArb/crypto_price_aggregator/domain/PriceTick.java#22-101) and `PriceServiceImpl`
- Created helper methods in tests to avoid duplication

### KISS
- Straightforward arbitrage detection algorithm
- No over-engineering or premature optimization

### YAGNI
- Implemented only what's needed for arbitrage detection
- Deferred WebSocket and security features

